    {
        "content": "<p>nv3ifu opened <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14797\">PR #14797</a> from <code>nv3ifu:fix-laststores-perf-14312</code> to <code>bytecodealliance:main</code>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Hello, I have attempted to fix #14312.<br>\nIn the previous implementation, new extents were generated at branch merge points. This meant that even if a specific memory region had not been written to, the read operation following a merge could not reuse previous results, leading to redundant reads.<br>\nI have introduced a table to track extents for each memory region and added checks for writes occurring along the various paths leading up to a merge point. For regions that have not been modified—provided they pass the necessary state checks—the original markers are preserved, allowing existing optimization logic to eliminate redundant reads. A test case has also been added.<br>\nTesting locally with signals-based traps disabled—using the original <code>.wasm</code> program provided in the issue—execution time decreased by approximately 23%, while compilation time increased by about 0.9%.</p>\n<p>original text(Chinese,I am not good at English):<br>\n你好，我尝试修复了 #14312。<br>\n之前的代码会在分支汇合处生成新的 extent，导致即使某个内存区域没有被写过，汇合后的读取也可能无法复用之前的结果，进而重复读取。<br>\n我增加了一张按内存区域保存 extent 的表，并检查汇合前各条路径上的写入。对于没有被写过、且状态检查通过的区域，保留原来的标记，让已有的优化逻辑消除重复读取。同时补充了一个测试。<br>\n在 issue 提供的原始 .wasm 程序上，本地测试关闭 signals-based traps 后，执行耗时约减少 23%，编译耗时约增加 0.9%。</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 632633119,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1792270333
    },
