    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> fitzgen created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14797#discussion_r4351648478\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Blocks are generally dense and reachable, so we can avoid the cost of hashing for the outer map here. The inner maps are sparse, so they seem fine to leave as <code>FxHashMap</code>s.</p>\n<p><div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"suggestion\"><pre><span></span><code>    /// Regions written by each block before optimization, so eliminated stores\n    /// remain conservatively accounted for. `None` means a fence can clobber\n    /// every region.\n    block_clobbers: SecondaryMap&lt;Block, Option&lt;FxHashSet&lt;AliasRegion&gt;&gt;&gt;,\n</code></pre></div><br>\n</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 634055090,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1792692478
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> fitzgen created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14797#discussion_r4351628993\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Hard-coding <code>None</code> as the <code>region</code> argument to <code>extent_for</code> is done a few times, but requires that the <code>LastStore</code> is also not <code>Unknown</code>, or else this could lead to miscompiles. The existing call sites are sound, but this feels pretty subtle and like something we could easily accidentally mess up in the future.</p>\n<p>I think we could avoid this footgun by changing <code>extent_for</code> into something like this:</p>\n<p><div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Rust\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">fn</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">extent_for</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"o\">&amp;</span><span class=\"bp\">self</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">func</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kp\">&amp;</span><span class=\"nc\">Function</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">inst</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nc\">Inst</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">-&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">u32</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"k\">match</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">self</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">stores</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">get_last_store</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">func</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">inst</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">            </span><span class=\"c1\">// Each of these already names a version of memory all on its own,</span>\n<span class=\"w\">            </span><span class=\"c1\">// function wide, and so doesn't need an additional extent token.</span>\n<span class=\"w\">            </span><span class=\"n\">LastStore</span><span class=\"p\">::</span><span class=\"n\">NoStore</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">LastStore</span><span class=\"p\">::</span><span class=\"n\">Inst</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">_</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">NULL_EXTENT</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n\n<span class=\"w\">            </span><span class=\"c1\">// This one, on the other hand, only names a version of memory</span>\n<span class=\"w\">            </span><span class=\"c1\">// relative to the control-flow join that lost track of it.</span>\n<span class=\"w\">            </span><span class=\"n\">LastStore</span><span class=\"p\">::</span><span class=\"n\">Unknown</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">                </span><span class=\"fm\">debug_assert_ne!</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">self</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">extent</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">NULL_EXTENT</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">                </span><span class=\"n\">func</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">dfg</span>\n<span class=\"w\">                    </span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">insts</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"n\">inst</span><span class=\"p\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">                    </span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">alias_region</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"o\">&amp;</span><span class=\"n\">func</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">dfg</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">                    </span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">map_or</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">self</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">extent</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">|</span><span class=\"n\">region</span><span class=\"o\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">self</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">region_extents</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"n\">region</span><span class=\"p\">])</span>\n<span class=\"w\">            </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div><br>\n</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 634055091,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1792692478
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> fitzgen created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14797#discussion_r4351821969\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Please factor this out into helper method(s).</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 634055092,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1792692478
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> fitzgen created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14797#discussion_r4351751234\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>We could avoid allocating a hash set on every <code>push_scope</code> call to this function, if this instead</p>\n<ul>\n<li>took a <code>clobbers: &amp;mut FxHashSet&lt;AliasRegion&gt;</code> parameter</li>\n<li><code>debug_assert!(clobbers.is_empty())</code> at the start of the function</li>\n<li>returned <code>bool</code> describing whether the <code>clobbers</code> is sound or not (i.e. <code>false</code> is semantically equivalent to today's <code>None</code>)</li>\n</ul>\n<p>and then we would also add an <code>AliasAnalysis::clobbers_scratch: FxHashSet&lt;AliasRegion&gt;</code> field that we always use to pass to this function, <code>.clear()</code>ing it just before the call.</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 634055093,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1792692478
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> fitzgen created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14797#discussion_r4351804994\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Rather than cloning <code>region_extents</code> twice in <code>push_scope</code>, can we instead:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>clone it only once, for putting it into <code>Scope</code></li>\n<li>not have a <code>MemoryState::region_extents</code> field</li>\n<li>in the places where we access <code>MemoryState::region_extents</code> today, instead access <code>alias_analysis.scopes.last().unwrap().region_extents</code></li>\n</ul>\n<p>?</p>\n<p>This may require making <code>MemoryState</code> have a lifetime parameter and hold a reference to its <code>AliasAnalysis</code>, but I think that should be pretty straightforward. If not, then we can revisit.</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 634055094,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1792692478
    },
